static keyword
    Normally, every object gets its own copy of fields.
    static means: “this belongs to the class itself, not to any one object.”

Analogy: In a school, every student has their own roll number (instance),
    but the school name is the same for everyone (static). You don’t store the school name
    inside each student. You store it once.

Memory view:
    name lives inside each object on the heap. college is stored once at class level,
    created when the class is loaded, and shared by all objects.

static method -
    Called using the class name, with no object needed.
    Rules to remember:
    A static method cannot use "this".
    A static method cannot directly access non-static fields or methods, because there may be
    no object yet. It would not know which object’s data to use.
    A non-static method can access static members freely.

Static block -
    Runs once, when the class is first loaded, before main and before any object.

final keyword
    “this cannot be changed.” What exactly can’t change depends on where you use it.
Used on	             Meaning
Variable	        Value can’t be reassigned (a constant)
Method	            Can’t be overridden by a child class
Class	            Can’t be extended (no child classes)